observations :

stronger seasons such as 2018, 2019, 2021 and 2023 generally recorded higher chasing success rates.

Examples:

2018 → 80.00%
2019 → 63.64%
2021 → 100.00%
2023 → 57.14%

In contrast, weaker seasons such as 2022 and 2025 recorded significantly lower chasing win percentages.

Similarly, successful seasons consistently maintained defending win percentages of at least 50%, while weaker seasons often struggled to defend totals.

The most extreme example was 2025, where CSK won only 16.67% of matches when defending.


conclusion:

both chasing and defending performance appear to be important contributors to season success.

however, defending performance shows a clearer separation between successful and unsuccessful seasons.

weak CSK teams frequently struggled to convert defendable totals into victories, suggesting that bowling effectiveness and match control may have played a significant role in poor seasons.

this finding aligns with earlier bowling analysis, which showed relationships between team success and metrics such as total wickets, powerplay wickets and bowling economy rates.


